From 9893a1e079fc5ec476cf2c93a8f0c4cb09f1555f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Velox <velox@localhost>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 20:54:16 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] gfxstream: answer vkGetFenceStatus in the guest when possible

vkGetFenceStatus was a synchronous host round trip (about 33 us on WHPX
with the goldfish pipe), also for fences that the host had already
reported as signaled.

- Remember a host VK_SUCCESS (vkGetFenceStatus, waitAll
  vkWaitForFences) until vkResetFences; a signaled fence only becomes
  unsignaled by a reset.
- When a poll finds a fence unsignaled, ask the host through the
  goldfish sync device to signal a sync fd once that submission
  completed (type 0x56, the fence's submission number in the upper
  bits). Further polls check the fd locally. When the fd signals,
  confirm once with the host: the host also signals on timeout or
  error, and one timeline signals in order.
- Keep signal operation order: submissions are numbered, and every
  call that tells the guest that queue work completed (fence and
  semaphore waits, wait idle, query results, event status) raises the
  highest submission number the guest may know to be complete. A hint
  that has not fired only answers VK_NOT_READY for newer submissions.
  vkDeviceWaitIdle, vkWaitSemaphores, vkGetSemaphoreCounterValue,
  vkGetQueryPoolResults and vkGetEventStatus now go through
  ResourceTracker for that.

Requires ANDROID_EMU_vulkan_fence_status_hint from the host.
debug.velox.fence_hint=0 disables it; debug.velox.fence_stats=1 logs
call counts every 10 s.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: Ie3203807015a8460f38ed18c53fff2a493554826
---
